('734', 'IFcSg4YvuVlx56msjbdf', 'GOoQYuz81C5vy6YQy1kA', NULL, '650', 'Good Morning, Hedy

I hope you had a good weekend!

Please see my comments below

Outside of removing and installing the windows, what will you be doing to make good of the surrounding area when fitting We do not offer any paint or flooring touch ups - This is left to others as it is out of our remit. A painter will be best to contact to carry out the works (being minimal making good up top our frame)
What will you need to carryout in the space before the windows can be installed as this is not mentioned in the quote No preparation will be needed - The only thing that we will require is that furniture blocking the doors be moved to ensure there is no damage nor obstruction while working.
Due to us updating the windows/doors as the current ones in place are causing water ingress, what will be in place to prevent this with our new windows / sliding doors (Will there be something in place to protect from further leaks)? Apart form the new doors and roof light being made to handle weathering and what nit - The whole system is sealed with both silicone as well as the fabrication that includes drainage run offs and tracks.
Can you confirm if the trim around the edges of the windows be replaced This again is something that is out of our remit - Once we have fit the doors as fabricated within the opening - Should trims be required - these can be ordered to finish off where needed (this will be identified on survey)
Please can you send over any technical drawings (if you have them yet) so that we can visually see the framework Drawings showing the systems and what they will look like would be issued to yourself on commencement
Do you supply triple glazing? We’d love to future proof our glass windows and doors and would be interested in this if it’s something you offer We can certainly offer triple glazing on both the sliding doors and roof light (if you would like me to have the quotation updated please let me know - One thing to be mindful of is that in doing so - The weight of the glass will likely exceed the 100kg limit and a crane would need to be arrranged (which we can do) to lift this in place)
To confirm that all waste (insisting windows) will be removed after the installation I can confirm that all materials and waste will be removed by ourselves', '3xDKaRc10kK7kAywVUTA', '2026-06-15 09:29:38+00', 't', 'Deposit & Sales Contract', '2.1340799537037037', NULL, '2026-09-25 10:49:42.918134+00', 'misha_full_run'),
