('828', 'kHcvavc8fEeqkEPTK2T8', 'Di4AVypPkgi1m8f1VHX6', NULL, '770', 'Hi Ben,

Thanks for your email and for the photos and dimensions.

I have attached your quotation to this email for you along with the Crittall window profile details and brochure.

Option 1 is what most of our clients use and we have used on a large number of listed buildings and it is also the cheapest option, this option is for cosmetic bars on faces 1-4 with a duplex spacer to give a true bar look.

Option 2 is for true steel glazing bars and each glass pane is individual, as you will see this option is a lot more expensive due to more steel being used and the individual glass panes.

We do have a £5000 + VAT minimum order value so if it was just the one window and in cosmetic bars we would need to look at seeing if there were any more windows in need of being replaced to meet the minimum order value.

Please let me know if you have any questions.

I look forward to hearing from you.

